 ## Overview
-Global-Local Contrastive Learning is a regularization strategy for text-driven NeRF stylization that controls stylization strength by combining global and local contrastive terms in CLIP space [S1]. It ensures uniform stylization across the entire scene, overcoming the directional-only limitation of standard CLIP losses and the non-uniformity of global-only approaches [S1]. It builds on [CLIP Direction Consistency](12264-clip-direction-consistency.md) by adding magnitude control and local balance.
+Global-Local Contrastive Learning is a regularization strategy for text-driven NeRF stylization that controls stylization strength by combining global and local contrastive terms in CLIP space [S1]. It ensures uniform stylization across the entire scene, overcoming the directional-only limitation of standard CLIP losses and the non-uniformity of global-only approaches [S1]. It builds on [CLIP Direction Consistency](12264-clip-direction-consistency.md) by adding magnitude control and local balance [S1].
 
